From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] run-openwrt: no queue starts while hardware offloading (WED) is on

With MilkFlint's hardware offloading with Wireless Ethernet Dispatch on
(milkflint.wifi.wed), the SoC forwards established connections by itself:
their packets reach no qdisc, so a queue would shape only what's left, as
if that were the whole line. The setting turns the queues off in the config
(and back on with it), but a queue set to run by hand, by LuCI between two
reloads or by a restored backup would still start.

A start now leaves such a queue alone and says why in the log. The VPN's
queue (wg_out) starts as before: what goes into the tunnel is never
forwarded in hardware.

--- a/src/run-openwrt.sh
+++ b/src/run-openwrt.sh
@@ -111,6 +111,15 @@
     [ -z "$RUN_IFACE" -o "$RUN_IFACE" = "$IFACE" ] || return
     [ "$(config_get "$section" enabled)" -eq 1 ] || return 0
     [ -f "${SQM_STATE_DIR}/${IFACE}.state" ] && return
+    # MilkFlint: with hardware offloading (WED) on, the SoC forwards
+    # established connections by itself, past every queue; only the VPN's,
+    # inside its tunnel, still sees all of its traffic. A queue set to run
+    # all the same (uci by hand, a restored backup) doesn't start, and says
+    # why.
+    if [ "$IFACE" != wg_out ] && [ "$(uci -q get milkflint.wifi.wed)" = 1 ]; then
+        sqm_warn "${IFACE}: not started. Hardware offloading (WED) is on, and the connections it forwards would pass this queue by: turn WED off to use it."
+        return 0
+    fi

     export UPLINK=$(config_get "$section" upload)
     export DOWNLINK=$(config_get "$section" download)
